/* The example captures, built by repos/flood-watch/tests/make_examples.py.

   Synthetic, and the page says so. Synthetic does not have to mean fake
   looking: gaps between packets are exponential, TTLs come from real
   starting values minus a hop count, ports come from the right ephemeral
   ranges, and every one has ordinary traffic running underneath, because
   a capture containing nothing but an attack is a capture nobody has ever
   taken. Each is gzipped, then base64, and unpacked in the browser. */
